      "text": "(a)Note that from Vieta's formulas,\n$a+b+c=-3, ab+bc+ca=4$, and $abc=11.$\n\n(b)Now, note that\n$$a+b+c=(a+b+c)^2=a^2+b^2+c^2+2(ab+bc+ca),$$\nwhich implies\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\sum_{\\text{cyc}}a+b+c&=a^2+b^2+c^2+2\\cdot4,\\\\ &=(a^2+ab+b^2)+(b^2+bc+c^2)+(c^2+ca+a^2)+8.\\\\ &=(a+b+c)^2+(a+b+c)+8.\\end{aligned}$$\n\n(c)Hence, from part (a), $24+3+t=9$, which gives $\\boxed{\\boxed{t=-15}}$.The answer is: -15",
