    {
      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "We can complete the Resultant to find a quartic equation whose roots are $a+b$, $b+c$, $c+a$, and $a+b+c$. This polynomial is $P(x) = x^4 + 6x^3 - 17x^2 - 21x + 52$. We deduce $t$ from the Rational Root Theorem by looking for factors of 52 that add up to 17. (No, $P(1)$ is not a zero of $P$. We shall see.)  Since $52 = 4\\cdot13$ and $17 = 13+4$,  $a+b+c = 13$ and $P(13)=0$, corresponding to $t=\\boxed{-23}$. Since we can require $P(4)=0$, which folds into $t=17$, we get $$P(x)=x^4 + 6x^3 + \\bbox[5px,border:1px solid #f00]{9x^2} + \\bbox[5px,border:1px solid #f00]{6x} + 52.\\tag*$0=P(13)$ provides no surprise: substituting $x=13$ looks an awful lot like the third equation in $*$, which isn't entirely surprising, given that $$\\frac1xP\\Bigl(\\frac1x\\Bigr)=\\frac1{x^4}$$Appealing to the Rational Root Theorem explicitly tries to find p/r such that $P\\bigl(\\tfrac p r\\bigr)=0$, forcing $r=p$ and $x=\\tfrac1x$, likewise wont help, and might even end up landing in a situation where something else is nonzero.  Were forced to invoke Halmos (\"proportional\"): definition22, but that would keep the appearance of giving all the factors.  Perhaps the dream of staying with arithmetic is causing problems.\n\nI must admit that such proof is tedious,...\n13^3+17×13^2+21×13-11\n.........=9×(13)\n............=1185\n--------------=17\n.......52\nLet us use another RFT theorem to handle the problem.\n\nBy the Remainder Theorem, when evaluating a polynomial we can subtract the given value and the roots to find the roots equal to 0. This allows us to divide 13 from the expression above (remains 52) to reduce the equation into an isoamorphic polynomial = R(a,b,c)=(0,0,13). This is then inspected when applied to the factors of 52 and the Sum of Roots 13*13/2*1=17.\n\n17=-23 means what?\n\nAlternative solution: I didn't like the fancy notation; numbers are fine.\n$$P-23(x-13)=10(x-4)(x-3)(x-1)(x+1)$$But for simplicity, we could have also said:\n$$10(x-4)(x-1)=10x(x-3)$$\n\nWriting x as (y+z) and solving now gives $a+b=1$, $b+c=2$, and $c+a=3$. This trivially implies $a-b=-1$, $b-c=-2$, and $c-a=1$, which implies $a+b+c=1$, implying $t=1185 - 9(x+13)=1185-423=1752$.",
